ae2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": false, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "ed.\n\n**Root cause:** `settings.json:2` has `\"rat\": 0.5` where it should say `\"fee_rate\": 0.5`.\n\n**Why the total comes out wrong:**\n- `main.py:10-13` looks up `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]`.\n- That raises a `KeyError`, which the code catches. It then sets `rate = 0` without any warning.\n- So `python3 main.py` prints `Total: 0` instead of `Total: 5.0` (0.5 \u00d7 `COUNT = 10`, set at `main.py:5`).\n\n**Suggested fixes:**\n1. Rename the key in `settings.json` to `\"fee_rate\"`.\n2. Optionally, replace the silent `rate = 0` fallback in `main.py:12-13` with an explicit error. `billing/report.py` already does this with `raise SystemExit(\"fee_rate is missing\")`.\n\nShould I apply either fix?\n[tool: grep]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\nThe settings key is read in three places. All of them look for `fee_rate`, and nothing reads `\"rat\"`, so fixing the key in `settings.json` covers all three.\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nI fixed the bug by renaming the misspelled key in `settings.json` from `\"rat\"` to `\"fee_rate\"`, and all three places that read the setting now work.\n\n**Where the setting is read:**\n\n| File:line | Code | Before the fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `main.py:11` | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]` | Silently used 0 and printed `Total: 0` |\n| `billing/report.py:7` | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")` | Exited with \"fee_rate is missing\" |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")` | Exited with \"fee_rate is missing\" |\n\nThe subagent missed the CSV writer: the key is split into two strings there, so a plain search for `fee_rate` doesn't find it. Nothing in the codebase reads `\"rat\"`, so renaming it can't break anything.\n\n**After the fix:**\n```\npython3 main.py                    -> Total: 5.0\npython3 -m billing.report          -> Report fee: 0.5\npython3 -m billing.export.csv_writer -> CSV fee: 0.5\n```\n\n`main.py:12-13` still sets the rate to 0 without warning if the key is missing, so a future typo would hide the same way. Should I change it to fail loudly like the other two scripts do?", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 7, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 94428, "requests_cache_write": 55251, "requests_cost_usd": 0.37552860000000005, "requests_count": 13, "requests_input_uncached": 1547, "requests_output": 3710, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial19", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 72, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T05:20:26.381187+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 1, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 45.177, "t_checker_s": 0.225, "t_env_setup_s": 0.003, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 5257, "tokens_cache_read": 94428, "tokens_cache_write": 55251, "tokens_fresh": 2253, "tokens_input_uncached": 1547, "tokens_main_cache_read": 70548, "tokens_main_cache_write": 35762, "tokens_main_calls": 6, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_output": 2237, "tokens_output": 3710, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 94428, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 55251, "tokens_proxy_calls": 13, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 1547, "tokens_proxy_output": 3710, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchai